---

An event file is small. It needs a `commands_poll`. Everything else is flavor.

- `activation`: `walk_through`, `touch`, `stepped_on`
- `persistent`: one-shot or it can fire again
- `command_location`: `free` (the player) or `event_location` (your orange markers)
- `command_location_range`: how far to look for those markers (default 32)

**free** is “run this as the player who tripped it.” Good for a tellraw, a title, giving an item.

**event_location** is “run this once per matching orange marker in range, standing on that block.” Good for filling a cauldron, opening a door two blocks away, summoning a mob in the pit, not on the player’s head.

If you stamp the same corridor six times and reuse the ids, **range** keeps each copy local. A one-shot in room A does not eat room B.

A first event people actually ship: walk through a tripwire-looking air block, play a sound, `setblock` a barrier out of the way. Poll has one command. Event is `walk_through`, one-shot, `free` or `event_location` depending on where the door sits.
